# Code quality — <PROJECT_NAME>

This document sets the quality rules **specific to this project**. It is
normative: it states what the project requires, not what the code does
today (that is the handbook's job). The code audit (`/clean-code`)
reads it before any other context.

What does not belong here:

- the *why* of a structural decision → an ADR, linked from this file;
- the description of the implementation → the handbook;
- rules already enforced by a tool's configuration → point to the
  configuration file, do not copy it;
- generic principles (SOLID, Clean Code) → already in the audit
  skill.

